Web Fonts code

The Plug-In inside Web Fonts that draws Mill Serif and Mill Mono from 18
point up, from the outlines Web Fonts carries ('Msfn' resources, listed in
'Mfnt' 128). tools/extras/build.py puts it in the file as MPlg 128 with its
MIfc; Web Fonts is never a Plug-In file of its own.

A letter is drawn the first time a page needs it at a size, and kept: up to
24K of letters in all, in purgeable handles, and given back when memory is
short. Fonts are read from the file's resource fork a letter at a time.
Bold italic is the italic made one pixel bolder, as QuickDraw makes bold.
Lines are as tall as each outline's ascender, descender, and line gap
('hhea') make them at the size.

The engine (tt.h, parse.c, raster.c, glyph.c, strike.c) is written from
Apple's TrueType Reference Manual: no hinting, nonzero winding, dropout
control (TT_DROPOUT), integer arithmetic for the 68000. strike.c, a whole
'FONT' at once, isn't linked.

Build: ./build.sh writes build/Web Fonts.flt (-Os, 68000).
